confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Stephanie Bice (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Stephanie Bice enters the general election as a heavy favorite in a district that leans Republican by about nine points. She holds a commanding financial advantage, with roughly $2 million on hand compared to about $17,000 for Democrat Jena Nelson, and carries a Trump endorsement into the fall. Rating outlets overwhelmingly place the race in the Safe or Solid Republican column.\n\nThere are some signs of Democratic interest: Nelson won her primary, a Democratic-sponsored poll showed her trailing by only five points, and national Democrats have signaled investment in the district. Still, with no independent polling confirmation and Bice's structural advantages, the race remains firmly in Republican hands barring a major shift in the environment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -10.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0638, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1454, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0909, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1152, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.0}]}